<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ariane64-le04-2026-11-24 ascent (published-knot surrogate)</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-24: T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-24T11:14:52Z (+1792 s from the window open 2026-11-24T10:45:00Z). Arianespace: 24 November 2026 at 8:14 am local time in Kourou, 36 Amazon Leo satellites delivered to about 460 km, last satellite separation 2 hours 4 minutes after liftoff (https://newsroom.arianespace.com/arianespace-successfully-launches-another-36-amazon-leo-satellites-on-ariane-6s-10th-flight/?lang=eng). The minute is Arianespace&#x27;s; the second is LL2&#x27;s. LL2 id 7bdc412b-c965-4517-a131-f57a01189803, Launch Successful, net 2026-11-24T11:14:52Z, second precision, last_updated 2026-11-24T13:51:20Z. The published window was 10:45-11:14Z; liftoff is 52 s after that close. utc shifted +1792 s. ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. Deploy time not moved: the sim still ends at ESA&#x27;s deployment start T+5969 s. Arianespace&#x27;s flown last separation is 2 h 4 min. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Ariane 64 Block 2 VA271 / Amazon Leo LE-04 (ELA-4) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. T0 is the window open 2026-11-24T10:45:00Z (t0_kind window_open), window to 2026-11-24T11:14:00Z. RETIMED +84960 s from 2026-11-23T11:09:00Z; ECEF geometry unchanged.
Arianespace 24 Nov press release: 10:45-11:14 UTC (07:45-08:14 Kourou, 11:45-12:14 Paris). The 23 Nov window 11:09-11:38 UTC was scrubbed (ground support systems, before gantry removal). LL2 id 7bdc412b-c965-4517-a131-f57a01189803, Go, net 10:45:00Z, last_updated 2026-11-23T13:40:20Z.
TIME CONFLICT: ESA&#x27;s timeline column is labelled CET, but liftoff 11:09:22 matches UTC (Arianespace 12:09 Paris; ESA also writes 11:09-11:38 GMT). T0 is the window open, not 11:09:22.
Event times are ESA VA271 offsets: booster sep 143 s, fairing 192 s, core MECO 465 s, Vinci cutoff 1 1071 s.
Altitude knots (t s: km): 0:0 (pad); 143:87 BORROWED from NASASpaceflight LE-01 booster sep (~T+2:25, P120C, 32 sats, not this flight); 192:127 BORROWED from the same LE-01 fairing note (~T+3:11); 465:275 generic ArianeGroup &#x27;Vulcain burns up to an altitude of around 275 km&#x27;, not this flight; 1071:150 ASSUMED transfer height (the fit target at Vinci cutoff 1). No VA271 altitude table is published.
Between knots the altitude is linear. From MECO (275 km, generic) down to 150 km at T+1071 is that interpolation, not a published transfer shape.
Horizontal ground speed ASSUMED linear from 0 to 7.527 km/s at T+1071 s. That end speed is circular inertial speed at 150 km (7.814 km/s) minus Earth rotation at the pad along azimuth 37.23 deg. The stage is not in a circular orbit at T+1071. This is the one horizontal-motion assumption.
File ends at Vinci cutoff 1. The second Vinci burn (T+4012 to T+4030) and deployment (starts T+5969, ends T+7719) are on the sim file, not this rhumb. Arianespace's 24 Nov release says final satellite separation about 2 h 4 min after liftoff (~T+7440 s). That figure is not this file's end. The sim still ends at ESA's deployment start T+5969 s.
Azimuth 37.23 deg: mean bearing from ELA-4 to the vertex-average centroids of NAVAREA IV 1118/26 areas A (37.30 deg, 823 km) and B (37.17 deg, 976 km). HYDROLANT 2324/26 centroid bears 37.05 deg at 3373 km and was not averaged in. Non-rotating inclination from 37.23 deg is 52.95 deg. Not retuned toward the 51.9 deg Amazon Leo shell (that azimuth would be 38.29 deg).
Pad (LL2 Ariane Launch Area 4): 5.256319N -52.786838E, altitude 0 m ASSUMED. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth spherical rhumb, R=6371.0088 km. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-24T11:14:52Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
